The dashboard ships no static assets today, but its Dockerfile COPYs this
directory the same way the storefront's does. Git does not track an empty
directory and Docker's build context does not carry one, so without this file
that COPY fails the image build outright — which is exactly how it failed.

Keeping the directory (rather than deleting the COPY) means the first asset
dropped in here is served with no Dockerfile change. Deleting the COPY would
make that same addition silently 404 in production instead.
